module

public import TauCeti.LinearAlgebra.RootSystem.Weyl.Affine.Alcove
import TauCeti.LinearAlgebra.RootSystem.Inversions.Length

/-!
# The closed fundamental alcove is a strict fundamental domain

Let `b` be a base of a finite, reduced, irreducible, crystallographic root pairing `P` over a
linearly ordered field `R`, with simple roots `αᵢ`, highest root `θ`, fundamental alcove `A`
(`RootPairing.fundamentalAlcove`), and closed fundamental alcove `Ā`
(`RootPairing.closedFundamentalAlcove`). Over an archimedean field, the translates of `Ā` under
the affine Weyl group `W_aff` (`RootPairing.affineWeylGroup`) cover the coweight space `N`
(`RootPairing.exists_mem_affineWeylGroup_apply_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove`). This file proves that
`Ā` is a *strict* fundamental domain for `W_aff`, identifies the point stabilizers in `W_aff` as
finite parabolic subgroups generated by wall reflections, and determines the stabilizers of the
facets and closed faces of `Ā`.

The central argument needs no archimedean hypothesis. Suppose `x ∈ Ā`, `f ∈ W_aff`, and `y = f x`
also lies in `Ā`. Pick a point `x₀ ∈ A`. Along the open segment `x_t = (1 - t) x + t x₀`
(`0 < t < 1`), every point `x_t` lies in `A`, and `f x_t = (1 - t) y + t f x₀` approaches `y`
linearly in each of the finitely many root functionals. Choosing `t` small enough ensures that
every positive affine root hyperplane separating `f x_t` from `A` already passes through `y`.
Local gallery descent
(`RootPairing.exists_mem_closure_affineWallReflections_apply_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove`)
then produces an element `g` in the subgroup generated by the wall reflections
`b.affineWallReflections y` through `y` such that `(g * f) x_t ∈ Ā`. Because `x_t ∈ A` avoids all
affine root hyperplanes, so does `(g * f) x_t`, whence `(g * f) x_t ∈ A`. By freeness of `W_aff` on
the open alcoves (`RootPairing.eq_one_of_mem_affineWeylGroup_of_apply_mem_fundamentalAlcove`),
`g * f = 1`, so `f = g⁻¹` is a product of wall reflections fixing `y = f x`. In particular
`f (f x) = f x`, which by injectivity of `f` forces `f x = x`, and simultaneously shows `f` lies in
the subgroup generated by `b.affineWallReflections x`.

From this single perturbation-and-gallery step we read off:
* **Uniqueness of closed-alcove representatives**: if `x ∈ Ā` and `f ∈ W_aff` has `f x ∈ Ā`, then
  `f x = x`, so over an archimedean field every `W_aff`-orbit meets `Ā` in a unique point.
* **Coxeter generation of `W_aff`**: over an archimedean field, `W_aff` is generated by the affine
  simple reflections `b.affineSimpleReflection`.
* **Parabolic point stabilizers**: for `x ∈ Ā`, the stabilizer `P.affinePointStabilizer x` in
  `W_aff` is finite and equals both `Subgroup.closure (b.affineWallReflections x)` and
  `Subgroup.closure (P.affineRootReflections x)`. By conjugation, at an arbitrary point `y : N`
  carried into `Ā` by `g ∈ W_aff`, the stabilizer of `y` is the `g⁻¹`-conjugate of the parabolic
  stabilizer of `g y`, and over an archimedean field every point stabilizer in `W_aff` is generated
  by the reflections in the affine root hyperplanes passing through that point.
* **Face stabilizers**: for a set `J` of nodes of the affine Dynkin diagram, the stabilizer in
  `W_aff` of every point of the open facet `b.openAlcoveFace J` (as well as the pointwise
  stabilizer of the closed face `b.closedAlcoveFace J` when `J ≠ univ`) is the parabolic subgroup
  `Subgroup.closure (b.affineSimpleReflection '' J)`, and distinct affine nodes define distinct
  affine simple reflections.

## Main definitions

* `RootPairing.affinePointStabilizer`: the stabilizer in `W_aff` of a point `x : N`.
* `RootPairing.affineRootReflections`: the reflections `s_{αⱼ,c}` (`c : ℤ`) in the affine root
  hyperplanes passing through `x`.

## Main results

* `RootPairing.closure_range_affineSimpleReflection`: over an archimedean linearly ordered field,
  the affine simple reflections generate `W_aff`.
* `RootPairing.finite_affinePointStabilizer_of_base` and
  `RootPairing.instFiniteAffinePointStabilizer`: point stabilizers in `W_aff` are finite.
* `RootPairing.mem_closure_affineWallReflections_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove` and
  `RootPairing.affinePointStabilizer_eq_closure_affineWallReflections`: **for `x ∈ Ā`, its
  stabilizer in `W_aff` is generated by the reflections in the walls of `A` passing through `x`.**
* `RootPairing.eq_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove_of_mem_affineWeylGroup` and
  `RootPairing.existsUnique_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove_and_exists_mem_affineWeylGroup`: **the
  closed fundamental alcove is a strict fundamental domain for `W_aff`.**
* `RootPairing.affinePointStabilizer_eq_map_conj_closure_affineWallReflections` and
  `RootPairing.affinePointStabilizer_eq_closure_affineRootReflections`: conjugation comparison and
  the root-hyperplane generation of arbitrary point stabilizers in `W_aff`.
* `RootPairing.Base.affineSimpleReflection_injective`,
  `RootPairing.affinePointStabilizer_eq_of_mem_openAlcoveFace`, and
  `RootPairing.iInf_affinePointStabilizer_closedAlcoveFace`: injectivity of
  `b.affineSimpleReflection` and parabolic stabilizers of facets and closed faces.

## References

* N. Bourbaki, *Lie Groups and Lie Algebras, Chapters 4–6*, Ch. V, §3.3 and Ch. VI, §2.1–§2.2.
* J. E. Humphreys, *Reflection Groups and Coxeter Groups*, Cambridge Studies in Advanced
  Mathematics 29, §4.3–§4.6.
* L. Garnier, *Affine Weyl groups and compact Lie groups*, §1.3, Theorem 1.3.5.
-/

public section

open Set Function

namespace RootPairing

/-! ### Point stabilizers and root-hyperplane reflections -/

section Stabilizer

variable {ι R M N : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [AddCommGroup N]
  [Module R N] (P : RootPairing ι R M N)

/-- The **point stabilizer** of `x : N` in the affine Weyl group: the subgroup of `W_aff`
consisting of elements fixing `x`. -/
def affinePointStabilizer (x : N) : Subgroup (N ≃ᵃ[R] N) where
  carrier := {f | f ∈ P.affineWeylGroup ∧ f x = x}
  one_mem' := ⟨one_mem _, rfl⟩
  mul_mem' hf hg := ⟨mul_mem hf.1 hg.1, by simp [hf.2, hg.2]⟩
  inv_mem' {f} hf :=
    ⟨inv_mem hf.1, by simpa [AffineEquiv.inv_def] using congrArg f.symm hf.2.symm⟩

@[simp]
lemma mem_affinePointStabilizer {x : N} {f : N ≃ᵃ[R] N} :
    f ∈ P.affinePointStabilizer x ↔ f ∈ P.affineWeylGroup ∧ f x = x :=
  Iff.rfl

lemma affinePointStabilizer_le_affineWeylGroup (x : N) :
    P.affinePointStabilizer x ≤ P.affineWeylGroup :=
  fun _ hf ↦ hf.1

/-- An affine automorphism fixing `x` is determined by its linear part, so `AffineEquiv.linearHom`
is injective on `P.affinePointStabilizer x`. -/
theorem linearHom_injOn_affinePointStabilizer (x : N) :
    InjOn (AffineEquiv.linearHom : (N ≃ᵃ[R] N) → _) (P.affinePointStabilizer x) :=
  fun _ ⟨_, hfx⟩ _ ⟨_, hgx⟩ hlin ↦ AffineEquiv.toAffineMap_injective
    (AffineMap.ext_linear (congrArg LinearEquiv.toLinearMap hlin) (hfx.trans hgx.symm))

/-- If the Weyl group of `P` is finite, the stabilizer of every point in `W_aff` is finite, as
`AffineEquiv.linearHom` embeds it into the coweight image of `P.weylGroup`. -/
theorem finite_affinePointStabilizer_of_finite_weylGroup [Finite P.weylGroup] (x : N) :
    Finite (P.affinePointStabilizer x) := by
  have hop_mem {w : N ≃ₗ[R] N} (hw : w ∈ Subgroup.closure (range P.coreflection)) :
      MulOpposite.op w ∈ MonoidHom.range ((Equiv.coweightHom P).domRestrict P.weylGroup) := by
    rw [P.range_weylGroup_coweightHom]
    induction hw using Subgroup.closure_induction with
    | mem _ h =>
      obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := h
      exact Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨i, rfl⟩
    | one => exact one_mem _
    | mul _ _ _ _ ih₁ ih₂ => exact mul_mem ih₂ ih₁
    | inv _ _ ih => exact inv_mem ih
  let _ : Finite (MonoidHom.range ((Equiv.coweightHom P).domRestrict P.weylGroup)) :=
    Finite.of_surjective _ ((Equiv.coweightHom P).domRestrict P.weylGroup).rangeRestrict_surjective
  let φ : P.affinePointStabilizer x →
      MonoidHom.range ((Equiv.coweightHom P).domRestrict P.weylGroup) :=
    fun f ↦ ⟨MulOpposite.op f.1.linear, hop_mem (P.mem_affineWeylGroup_iff.mp f.2.1).1⟩
  refine Finite.of_injective φ fun f g h ↦ Subtype.ext ?_
  exact P.linearHom_injOn_affinePointStabilizer x f.2 g.2
    (MulOpposite.op_injective (congrArg Subtype.val h))

/-- For a crystallographic reduced root pairing with finitely many roots and a base `b`, every
point stabilizer in `W_aff` is finite; the roots need not span. -/
theorem finite_affinePointStabilizer_of_base [Finite ι] [CharZero R] [IsDomain R]
    [P.IsCrystallographic] [P.IsReduced] (b : P.Base) (x : N) :
    Finite (P.affinePointStabilizer x) := by
  let _ : Finite P.weylGroup := P.finite_weylGroup_of_base b
  exact P.finite_affinePointStabilizer_of_finite_weylGroup x

/-- For a finite root system, every point stabilizer in the affine Weyl group is finite. -/
instance instFiniteAffinePointStabilizer [Finite ι] [P.IsRootSystem] (x : N) :
    Finite (P.affinePointStabilizer x) := by
  let _ : Finite P.weylGroup := P.finite_weylGroup
  exact P.finite_affinePointStabilizer_of_finite_weylGroup x

/-- **The stabilizer of the origin in `W_aff` is the finite Weyl group**: the subgroup generated by
the coreflections `s_{αᵢ}`. -/
theorem affinePointStabilizer_zero :
    P.affinePointStabilizer 0 =
      Subgroup.closure (range fun i ↦ (P.coreflection i).toAffineEquiv) := by
  let toAff : (N ≃ₗ[R] N) →* (N ≃ᵃ[R] N) :=
    { toFun := LinearEquiv.toAffineEquiv
      map_one' := rfl
      map_mul' := fun _ _ ↦ rfl }
  have htoAff (w : N ≃ₗ[R] N) : toAff w = w.toAffineEquiv := rfl
  have hcl : Subgroup.closure (range fun i ↦ (P.coreflection i).toAffineEquiv) =
      (Subgroup.closure (range P.coreflection)).map toAff := by
    rw [MonoidHom.map_closure, ← range_comp]
    exact congrArg Subgroup.closure (congrArg range (funext fun i ↦ (htoAff _).symm))
  rw [hcl]
  ext f
  simp only [mem_affinePointStabilizer, Subgroup.mem_map]
  refine ⟨fun ⟨hf, hf0⟩ ↦ ⟨f.linear, (P.mem_affineWeylGroup_iff.mp hf).1, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · ext y
    rw [htoAff, LinearEquiv.coe_toAffineEquiv, AffineEquiv.apply_eq_linear_add f y, hf0, add_zero]
  · rintro ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨P.toAffineEquiv_mem_affineWeylGroup hw, map_zero w⟩

/-- Conjugating `P.affinePointStabilizer x` by `g ∈ W_aff` gives `P.affinePointStabilizer (g x)`. -/
theorem map_conj_affinePointStabilizer {g : N ≃ᵃ[R] N} (hg : g ∈ P.affineWeylGroup) (x : N) :
    (P.affinePointStabilizer x).map (MulAut.conj g).toMonoidHom =
      P.affinePointStabilizer (g x) := by
  ext h
  simp only [Subgroup.mem_map, mem_affinePointStabilizer, MulEquiv.coe_toMonoidHom,
    MulAut.conj_apply]
  refine ⟨?_, fun ⟨hh, hgx⟩ ↦
    ⟨g⁻¹ * h * g, ⟨mul_mem (mul_mem (inv_mem hg) hh) hg, ?_⟩, by group⟩⟩
  · rintro ⟨f, ⟨hf, hfx⟩, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨mul_mem (mul_mem hg hf) (inv_mem hg), by simp [AffineEquiv.inv_def, hfx]⟩
  · simpa [AffineEquiv.inv_def, mul_assoc] using congrArg g.symm hgx

/-- The affine reflections `s_{αⱼ,c}` (`c : ℤ`) in the affine root hyperplanes passing through
`x`. -/
def affineRootReflections (x : N) : Set (N ≃ᵃ[R] N) :=
  {s | ∃ (j : ι) (c : ℤ), P.root' j x = c ∧ P.affineCoreflection j c = s}

@[simp]
lemma mem_affineRootReflections {x : N} {s : N ≃ᵃ[R] N} :
    s ∈ P.affineRootReflections x ↔
      ∃ (j : ι) (c : ℤ), P.root' j x = c ∧ P.affineCoreflection j c = s :=
  Iff.rfl

lemma affineRootReflections_subset_affinePointStabilizer (x : N) :
    P.affineRootReflections x ⊆ P.affinePointStabilizer x := by
  rintro _ ⟨j, c, hjx, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨P.affineCoreflection_mem_affineWeylGroup j c,
    P.affineCoreflection_apply_of_root'_eq hjx⟩

lemma closure_affineRootReflections_le_affinePointStabilizer (x : N) :
    Subgroup.closure (P.affineRootReflections x) ≤ P.affinePointStabilizer x :=
  (Subgroup.closure_le _).mpr (P.affineRootReflections_subset_affinePointStabilizer x)

/-- Every wall reflection of a base `b` at `x` is a root-hyperplane reflection at `x`. -/
lemma Base.affineWallReflections_subset_affineRootReflections {P : RootPairing ι R M N}
    [CharZero R] [Finite ι] [Nonempty ι] (b : P.Base) (x : N) :
    b.affineWallReflections x ⊆ P.affineRootReflections x := by
  intro s hs
  obtain ⟨k, hk, rfl⟩ := b.mem_affineWallReflections.mp hs
  rcases k with _ | i
  · rw [Base.affineSimpleRoot_none] at hk
    exact ⟨b.highestRoot, 1, by simpa using (sub_eq_zero.mp hk).symm, by simp⟩
  · exact ⟨i, 0, by simpa using hk, by simp⟩

lemma Base.closure_affineWallReflections_le_affinePointStabilizer {P : RootPairing ι R M N}
    [CharZero R] [Finite ι] [Nonempty ι] (b : P.Base) (x : N) :
    Subgroup.closure (b.affineWallReflections x) ≤ P.affinePointStabilizer x :=
  (Subgroup.closure_mono (b.affineWallReflections_subset_affineRootReflections x)).trans
    (P.closure_affineRootReflections_le_affinePointStabilizer x)

/-- **Conjugating an affine reflection by an element of `W_aff` gives an affine reflection in the
image hyperplane.** -/
theorem exists_conj_affineCoreflection_eq [P.IsCrystallographic] {g : N ≃ᵃ[R] N}
    (hg : g ∈ P.affineWeylGroup) (j : ι) (c : ℤ) :
    ∃ (j' : ι) (c' : ℤ), g * P.affineCoreflection j c * g⁻¹ = P.affineCoreflection j' c' ∧
      ∀ x, P.root' j' (g x) - c' = P.root' j x - c := by
  obtain ⟨j', m, hm⟩ := P.exists_root'_apply_eq_add_intCast_of_mem_affineWeylGroup (inv_mem hg) j
  refine ⟨j', c - m, ?_, fun x ↦ ?_⟩
  · have hlin : ∀ y, P.root' j (g⁻¹.linear y) = P.root' j' y := fun y ↦ by
      have hy := hm y
      have h0 := hm 0
      rw [AffineEquiv.apply_eq_linear_add g⁻¹ y, map_add] at hy
      simp only [map_zero, zero_add] at h0
      linear_combination hy - h0
    have hcor : g.linear (P.coroot j) = P.coroot j' := by
      have hinv := P.apply_coroot_eq_of_root'_apply_eq
        (P.mem_affineWeylGroup_iff.mp (inv_mem hg)).1 hlin
      have hll : g.linear (g⁻¹.linear (P.coroot j')) = P.coroot j' := by
        rw [AffineEquiv.inv_def, AffineEquiv.linear_symm, LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
      exact (congrArg g.linear hinv).symm.trans hll
    have hsub (u : N) (r : R) (v : N) : g (u - r • v) = g u - r • g.linear v := by
      rw [AffineEquiv.apply_eq_linear_add g (u - r • v), AffineEquiv.apply_eq_linear_add g u,
        map_sub, map_smul]
      abel
    ext y
    have hroot : P.root' j (g.symm y) - c = P.root' j' y - (c - m : ℤ) := by
      push_cast
      linear_combination hm y
    simp [affineCoreflection_apply_eq_sub, AffineEquiv.inv_def, hsub, hcor, hroot]
  · have hx := hm (g x)
    simp only [AffineEquiv.inv_def, AffineEquiv.symm_apply_apply] at hx
    push_cast
    linear_combination -hx

/-- Conjugation by `g ∈ W_aff` sends the root-hyperplane reflections fixing `x` onto those fixing
`g x`. -/
theorem image_conj_affineRootReflections [P.IsCrystallographic] {g : N ≃ᵃ[R] N}
    (hg : g ∈ P.affineWeylGroup) (x : N) :
    MulAut.conj g '' P.affineRootReflections x = P.affineRootReflections (g x) := by
  ext s
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨_, ⟨j, c, hjx, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨j', c', hconj, hroot⟩ := P.exists_conj_affineCoreflection_eq hg j c
    refine ⟨j', c', sub_eq_zero.mp ?_, hconj.symm⟩
    rw [hroot x, hjx, sub_self]
  · rintro ⟨j, c, hjgx, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨j', c', hconj, hroot⟩ := P.exists_conj_affineCoreflection_eq (inv_mem hg) j c
    refine ⟨P.affineCoreflection j' c', ⟨j', c', sub_eq_zero.mp ?_, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
    · have h := hroot (g x)
      simpa [AffineEquiv.inv_def, hjgx] using h
    · simp only [MulAut.conj_apply, ← hconj]
      group

end Stabilizer

/-! ### Strict fundamental domain and parabolic point stabilizers -/

section FundamentalDomain

variable {ι R M N : Type*} [Field R] [LinearOrder R] [IsStrictOrderedRing R]
  [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N]
  {P : RootPairing ι R M N} (b : P.Base)
  [Finite ι] [Nonempty ι] [P.IsCrystallographic] [P.IsReduced] [P.IsIrreducible]

/-- **Coxeter generation of `W_aff`**: over an archimedean linearly ordered field, the affine Weyl
group is generated by the affine simple reflections `b.affineSimpleReflection`. -/
theorem closure_range_affineSimpleReflection [Archimedean R] :
    Subgroup.closure (range b.affineSimpleReflection) = P.affineWeylGroup := by
  refine le_antisymm b.closure_range_affineSimpleReflection_le_affineWeylGroup fun f hf ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨x₀, hx₀⟩ := fundamentalAlcove_nonempty b
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hgfx⟩ :=
    exists_mem_closure_range_affineSimpleReflection_apply_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove b (f x₀)
  have hgf : g * f ∈ P.affineWeylGroup :=
    mul_mem (b.closure_range_affineSimpleReflection_le_affineWeylGroup hg) hf
  have hfeq : f = g⁻¹ := eq_inv_of_mul_eq_one_right
    (eq_one_of_mem_affineWeylGroup_of_apply_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove b hgf hx₀ hgfx)
  exact hfeq ▸ inv_mem hg

/-- Small-perturbation step: for `y` in the closed fundamental alcove and any point `z₀`, at a
sufficiently small `t ∈ (0, 1)` every positive affine root hyperplane separating
`AffineMap.lineMap y z₀ t` from the fundamental alcove passes through `y`. -/
private lemma exists_pos_lt_one_forall_root'_lineMap_eq {y : N}
    (hy : y ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b) (z₀ : N) :
    ∃ t : R, 0 < t ∧ t < 1 ∧
      ∀ (j : ι) (k : ℤ), (k < 0 ∨ k = 0 ∧ 0 < b.height j) →
        P.root' j (AffineMap.lineMap y z₀ t) < k → P.root' j y = k := by
  let _ := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  -- For each root `j`, bound the step size so `t * (|αⱼ(z₀ - y)| + 1)` stays below `1`, below
  -- `αⱼ(y)` when `αⱼ(y) > 0`, and below `αⱼ(y) + 1` when `αⱼ(y) > -1`; then take `t = m / 2`
  -- where `m` is the minimum of these positive bounds over the finitely many roots.
  let step (u : R) : R := if 0 < u then u else 1
  have hstep (u : R) : 0 < step u := by dsimp [step]; split_ifs with h <;> linarith
  let bound (j : ι) : R :=
    min 1 (min (step (P.root' j y + 1)) (step (P.root' j y))) / (|P.root' j (z₀ - y)| + 1)
  have hb_pos (j : ι) : 0 < bound j :=
    div_pos (lt_min one_pos (lt_min (hstep _) (hstep _))) (by positivity)
  have hb_le (j : ι) : bound j ≤ 1 :=
    (div_le_one (by linarith [abs_nonneg (P.root' j (z₀ - y))])).mpr
      ((min_le_left _ _).trans (by linarith [abs_nonneg (P.root' j (z₀ - y))]))
  let m := Finset.univ.inf' Finset.univ_nonempty bound
  have hm_pos : 0 < m := (Finset.lt_inf'_iff _).mpr fun j _ ↦ hb_pos j
  obtain ⟨j₀⟩ := ‹Nonempty ι›
  have hm_le : m ≤ 1 := (Finset.inf'_le _ (Finset.mem_univ j₀)).trans (hb_le j₀)
  refine ⟨m / 2, half_pos hm_pos, by linarith, fun j k hpos hlt ↦ ?_⟩
  have htm : (m / 2) * (|P.root' j (z₀ - y)| + 1) <
      min 1 (min (step (P.root' j y + 1)) (step (P.root' j y))) :=
    (lt_div_iff₀ (by positivity)).mp
      (lt_of_lt_of_le (half_lt_self hm_pos) (Finset.inf'_le bound (Finset.mem_univ j)))
  rw [AffineMap.lineMap_apply_module', map_add, map_smul, smul_eq_mul, add_comm] at hlt
  have hneg_abs : -(m / 2) * (|P.root' j (z₀ - y)| + 1) < (m / 2) * P.root' j (z₀ - y) := by
    nlinarith [neg_abs_le (P.root' j (z₀ - y)), half_pos hm_pos]
  -- Since `(j, k)` is a positive affine root, either `k = 0` (with `αⱼ` positive), `k = -1`, or
  -- `k ≤ -2`. On `Ā` we have `αⱼ(y) ≥ 0` for `αⱼ` positive and `αⱼ(y) ≥ -1` for every root.
  obtain rfl | rfl | hk2 : k = 0 ∨ k = -1 ∨ k ≤ -2 := by
    rcases hpos with hk | ⟨rfl, -⟩ <;> omega
  · -- Case `k = 0`: `αⱼ` is positive so `αⱼ(y) ≥ 0`; if `αⱼ(y) > 0`, the step keeps the segment
    -- positive, contradicting `hlt`.
    have hjpos : b.IsPos j := b.isPos_iff.mpr (hpos.resolve_left (by omega)).2
    rcases (mem_closedFundamentalAlcove_iff_forall_isPos.mp hy j hjpos).1.eq_or_lt with h0 | h0
    · simpa using h0.symm
    · have : (m / 2) * (|P.root' j (z₀ - y)| + 1) < P.root' j y := by
        simpa [step, h0] using (htm.trans_le (min_le_right _ _)).trans_le (min_le_right _ _)
      linarith
  · -- Case `k = -1`: `αⱼ(y) ≥ -1`; if `αⱼ(y) > -1`, the step keeps the segment above `-1`.
    rcases (neg_one_le_root'_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove hy j).eq_or_lt with h1 | h1
    · simpa using h1.symm
    · have h1' : 0 < P.root' j y + 1 := by linarith
      have : (m / 2) * (|P.root' j (z₀ - y)| + 1) < P.root' j y + 1 := by
        simpa [step, h1'] using (htm.trans_le (min_le_right _ _)).trans_le (min_le_left _ _)
      simp only [Int.cast_neg, Int.cast_one] at hlt
      linarith
  · -- Case `k ≤ -2`: impossible since `αⱼ(y) ≥ -1` and the perturbation changes `αⱼ` by `< 1`.
    have : (m / 2) * (|P.root' j (z₀ - y)| + 1) < 1 := htm.trans_le (min_le_left _ _)
    have hk2' : (k : R) ≤ -2 := by exact_mod_cast hk2
    linarith [neg_one_le_root'_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove hy j]

/-- Perturbation-and-gallery step: if `x ∈ Ā`, `f ∈ W_aff`, and `f x ∈ Ā`, then `f` lies in the
subgroup generated by the wall reflections at `f x`. -/
private lemma mem_closure_affineWallReflections_apply {x : N}
    (hx : x ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b) {f : N ≃ᵃ[R] N} (hf : f ∈ P.affineWeylGroup)
    (hfx : f x ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b) :
    f ∈ Subgroup.closure (b.affineWallReflections (f x)) := by
  obtain ⟨x₀, hx₀⟩ := fundamentalAlcove_nonempty b
  obtain ⟨t, ht₀, ht₁, hsep⟩ := exists_pos_lt_one_forall_root'_lineMap_eq b hfx (f x₀)
  set xt := AffineMap.lineMap x x₀ t
  have hxt : xt ∈ fundamentalAlcove P b := lineMap_mem_fundamentalAlcove hx hx₀ ht₀ ht₁
  have hfxt : f xt = AffineMap.lineMap (f x) (f x₀) t := f.apply_lineMap x x₀ t
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hgfxt⟩ :=
    exists_mem_closure_affineWallReflections_apply_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove b
      (y := f x) (z := f xt) (by simpa only [hfxt] using hsep)
  have hgf : g * f ∈ P.affineWeylGroup :=
    mul_mem ((b.closure_affineWallReflections_le_affinePointStabilizer (f x) hg).1) hf
  have hfeq : f = g⁻¹ := eq_inv_of_mul_eq_one_right
    (eq_one_of_mem_affineWeylGroup_of_apply_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove b hgf hxt hgfxt)
  have hg' : g⁻¹ ∈ Subgroup.closure (b.affineWallReflections (f x)) := inv_mem hg
  rwa [← hfeq] at hg'

/-- **Two points of the closed fundamental alcove in the same `W_aff`-orbit are equal**: if
`x ∈ Ā`, `f ∈ W_aff`, and `f x ∈ Ā`, then `f x = x`. -/
theorem eq_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove_of_mem_affineWeylGroup {x : N}
    (hx : x ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b) {f : N ≃ᵃ[R] N} (hf : f ∈ P.affineWeylGroup)
    (hfx : f x ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b) : f x = x :=
  f.injective ((b.closure_affineWallReflections_le_affinePointStabilizer (f x)
    (mem_closure_affineWallReflections_apply b hx hf hfx)).2)

/-- **An element of `W_aff` carrying a point `x` of the closed fundamental alcove into the closed
fundamental alcove is a product of reflections in the walls of the alcove passing through `x`.** -/
theorem mem_closure_affineWallReflections_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove {x : N}
    (hx : x ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b) {f : N ≃ᵃ[R] N} (hf : f ∈ P.affineWeylGroup)
    (hfx : f x ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b) :
    f ∈ Subgroup.closure (b.affineWallReflections x) := by
  have h := mem_closure_affineWallReflections_apply b hx hf hfx
  rwa [eq_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove_of_mem_affineWeylGroup b hx hf hfx] at h

/-- **Parabolic point stabilizer theorem**: for `x` in the closed fundamental alcove, its
stabilizer in `W_aff` is generated by the affine simple reflections in the walls of the alcove
passing through `x`. -/
theorem affinePointStabilizer_eq_closure_affineWallReflections {x : N}
    (hx : x ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b) :
    P.affinePointStabilizer x = Subgroup.closure (b.affineWallReflections x) :=
  le_antisymm
    (fun _ hf ↦ mem_closure_affineWallReflections_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove b hx hf.1
      (hf.2.symm ▸ hx))
    (b.closure_affineWallReflections_le_affinePointStabilizer x)

/-- For `x` in the closed fundamental alcove, its stabilizer in `W_aff` coincides with the subgroup
generated by all root-hyperplane reflections passing through `x`. -/
theorem affinePointStabilizer_eq_closure_affineRootReflections_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove
    {x : N} (hx : x ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b) :
    P.affinePointStabilizer x = Subgroup.closure (P.affineRootReflections x) :=
  le_antisymm
    ((affinePointStabilizer_eq_closure_affineWallReflections b hx).trans_le
      (Subgroup.closure_mono (b.affineWallReflections_subset_affineRootReflections x)))
    (P.closure_affineRootReflections_le_affinePointStabilizer x)

/-- Two elements of `W_aff` carrying the same point `x : N` into the closed fundamental alcove send
`x` to the same point. -/
theorem apply_eq_of_mem_affineWeylGroup_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove {f g : N ≃ᵃ[R] N}
    (hf : f ∈ P.affineWeylGroup) (hg : g ∈ P.affineWeylGroup) {x : N}
    (hfx : f x ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b) (hgx : g x ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b) :
    f x = g x := by
  have h := eq_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove_of_mem_affineWeylGroup b hfx
    (mul_mem hg (inv_mem hf)) (by simpa [AffineEquiv.inv_def] using hgx)
  simpa [AffineEquiv.inv_def] using h.symm

/-- **Conjugation comparison of point stabilizers**: if `g ∈ W_aff` carries `y : N` into the closed
fundamental alcove, the stabilizer of `y` in `W_aff` is the `g⁻¹`-conjugate of the parabolic wall
stabilizer of `g y`. -/
theorem affinePointStabilizer_eq_map_conj_closure_affineWallReflections {y : N} {g : N ≃ᵃ[R] N}
    (hg : g ∈ P.affineWeylGroup) (hgy : g y ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b) :
    P.affinePointStabilizer y =
      (Subgroup.closure (b.affineWallReflections (g y))).map (MulAut.conj g⁻¹).toMonoidHom := by
  have hy : g⁻¹ (g y) = y := by simp [AffineEquiv.inv_def]
  rw [← affinePointStabilizer_eq_closure_affineWallReflections b hgy,
    P.map_conj_affinePointStabilizer (inv_mem hg) (g y), hy]

/-- **The closed fundamental alcove is a strict fundamental domain for `W_aff`**: over an
archimedean linearly ordered field, every `W_aff`-orbit in `N` meets `closedFundamentalAlcove P b`
in a unique point. -/
theorem existsUnique_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove_and_exists_mem_affineWeylGroup [Archimedean R]
    (x : N) : ∃! y, y ∈ closedFundamentalAlcove P b ∧ ∃ f ∈ P.affineWeylGroup, f x = y := by
  obtain ⟨f, hf, hfx⟩ := exists_mem_affineWeylGroup_apply_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove b x
  refine ⟨f x, ⟨hfx, f, hf, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
  rintro _ ⟨hgy, g, hg, rfl⟩
  exact apply_eq_of_mem_affineWeylGroup_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove b hg hf hgy hfx

include b in
/-- **Every point stabilizer in `W_aff` is generated by the reflections in the affine root
hyperplanes passing through that point.** -/
theorem affinePointStabilizer_eq_closure_affineRootReflections [Archimedean R] (y : N) :
    P.affinePointStabilizer y = Subgroup.closure (P.affineRootReflections y) := by
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hgy⟩ := exists_mem_affineWeylGroup_apply_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove b y
  have hy : g⁻¹ (g y) = y := by simp [AffineEquiv.inv_def]
  calc P.affinePointStabilizer y
      = (P.affinePointStabilizer (g y)).map (MulAut.conj g⁻¹).toMonoidHom := by
        rw [P.map_conj_affinePointStabilizer (inv_mem hg) (g y), hy]
    _ = (Subgroup.closure (P.affineRootReflections (g y))).map
          (MulAut.conj g⁻¹).toMonoidHom := by
        rw [affinePointStabilizer_eq_closure_affineRootReflections_of_mem_closedFundamentalAlcove
          b hgy]
    _ = Subgroup.closure (MulAut.conj g⁻¹ '' P.affineRootReflections (g y)) :=
        MonoidHom.map_closure _ _
    _ = Subgroup.closure (P.affineRootReflections y) := by
        rw [P.image_conj_affineRootReflections (inv_mem hg) (g y), hy]

/-! ### Face stabilizers -/

/-- Distinct affine nodes define distinct affine simple reflections. -/
theorem Base.affineSimpleReflection_injective : Function.Injective b.affineSimpleReflection := by
  intro k l hkl
  by_contra hne
  have huniv : ({k} : Set (Option b.support)) ≠ univ := fun hu ↦
    hne (mem_singleton_iff.mp (hu ▸ mem_univ l)).symm
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := b.openAlcoveFace_nonempty_iff.mpr huniv
  obtain ⟨hx0, hxpos⟩ := b.mem_openAlcoveFace.mp hx
  have hsx : b.affineSimpleReflection l x = x := by
    rw [← hkl]
    exact b.affineSimpleReflection_apply_of_affineSimpleRoot_eq_zero (hx0 k rfl)
  exact (hxpos l (mem_singleton_iff.not.mpr (Ne.symm hne))).ne'
    ((b.affineSimpleReflection_apply_eq_self_iff).mp hsx)

/-- **Facet point stabilizer**: at any point `x` of the open facet `b.openAlcoveFace J`, the
stabilizer in `W_aff` is generated by the affine simple reflections indexed by `J`. -/
theorem affinePointStabilizer_eq_of_mem_openAlcoveFace {J : Set (Option b.support)} {x : N}
    (hx : x ∈ b.openAlcoveFace J) :
    P.affinePointStabilizer x = Subgroup.closure (b.affineSimpleReflection '' J) := by
  have hxbar := (b.mem_closedAlcoveFace.mp (b.openAlcoveFace_subset_closedAlcoveFace J hx)).1
  have hJ := Set.ext_iff.mp ((b.mem_openAlcoveFace_iff_eq_setOf_eq_zero hxbar).mp hx)
  rw [affinePointStabilizer_eq_closure_affineWallReflections b hxbar]
  congr 1
  ext s
  simp only [Base.mem_affineWallReflections, mem_image]
  exact exists_congr fun k ↦ and_congr_left' (hJ k)

/-- The stabilizer in `W_aff` of any point of the open fundamental alcove is trivial. -/
theorem affinePointStabilizer_eq_bot_of_mem_fundamentalAlcove {x : N}
    (hx : x ∈ fundamentalAlcove P b) : P.affinePointStabilizer x = ⊥ := by
  have hx' : x ∈ b.openAlcoveFace ∅ := by rwa [b.openAlcoveFace_empty]
  simpa using affinePointStabilizer_eq_of_mem_openAlcoveFace b hx'

/-- **Pointwise stabilizer of a nonempty closed face**: for `J ≠ univ`, the elements of `W_aff`
fixing every point of `b.closedAlcoveFace J` form the parabolic subgroup generated by
`b.affineSimpleReflection '' J`. -/
theorem iInf_affinePointStabilizer_closedAlcoveFace {J : Set (Option b.support)} (hJ : J ≠ univ) :
    (⨅ x ∈ b.closedAlcoveFace J, P.affinePointStabilizer x) =
      Subgroup.closure (b.affineSimpleReflection '' J) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (le_iInf₂ fun x hx ↦ (Subgroup.closure_le _).mpr ?_)
  · obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := b.openAlcoveFace_nonempty_iff.mpr hJ
    exact (biInf_le _ (b.openAlcoveFace_subset_closedAlcoveFace J hx)).trans_eq
      (affinePointStabilizer_eq_of_mem_openAlcoveFace b hx)
  · rintro _ ⟨k, hk, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨b.affineSimpleReflection_mem_affineWeylGroup k,
      b.affineSimpleReflection_apply_of_affineSimpleRoot_eq_zero
        ((b.mem_closedAlcoveFace.mp hx).2 k hk)⟩

end FundamentalDomain

